title: Capital Strike
subtitle: the Commonwealth's industries are idling...
view-if: (capital_strike_progress >= 10 or budget <= -5) and marcher_in_government
new-page: true
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: disfavored += 5; commons_marcher*= 0.7; burgher_marcher -= 15; guild_marcher -= 15; disfavored_marcher*=0.7; landed_marcher -= 15; pro_republic -= 15; capital_strike_seen = 1; unionist_relation -= 10; gold_relation -= 10; ddp_relation -= 8; lvp_relation -= 8; commons_royalist += 8; disfavored_royalist += 10; burgher_royalist += 15; guild_royalist += 15; landed_royalist += 15; gold_right += 5; ddp_right += 3; ddp_cohesion -= 1; lvp_right += 4; coalition_dissent += 1; dufour_angry += 100; economic_growth -= 4;
tags: event

= Capital Strike

Our policies have greatly angered the guild-masters. Investment has fallen, and workshops are idling, preventing the workers from fulfilling their jobs. Meanwhile, the propertied press is a constant chorus of venomous invective directed at us and our economic policies.

What can we do?

- @seize
- @capital_controls
- @propaganda
- @nothing

@seize
title: Empower workers to seize the workshops!
unavailable-subtitle: [? if left_strength <= reformist_strength + knight_strength : The bulk of the party does not support this radical action. ?] [? if judicial_reform < 3 : The judiciary would oppose this action. ?] [? if banner_militancy < 0.25 : If we increased the strength of our paramilitary forces, perhaps we could do this. ?] [? if works_councils < 1 : We need the support of the works councils first. ?]
choose-if: left_strength > reformist_strength + knight_strength and (judicial_reform >= 3 or banner_militancy >= 0.25) and works_councils >= 1
on-arrival: nationalization_progress += 1; coup_progress += 6; disfavored -= 2; disfavored -= 1 if works_councils >= 3; works_program += 1; commons_marcher += 10*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 10*(1-dissent); coalition_dissent += 2; gold_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 4; commons_royalist -= 8*(1-dissent); disfavored_royalist -= 8*(1-dissent); left_strength += 15; reformist_dissent += 10; left_dissent -= 10; factory_takeovers += 1; gold_right += 5; ddp_right += 3; lvp_right += 4; economic_growth += 2;

If the guild-masters are going to attack us, then we must hit them back. We have empowered the workers to seize and take full control of the workshops that the guild-masters have idled. The <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Sovereigntists</span>, of course, call us thieves and looters.


@capital_controls
title: Enact capital controls to lessen the impact.
choose-if: judicial_reform >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: The judiciary would never allow this.
on-arrival: disfavored -= 1.5; commons_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); economic_growth += 2;

Capital controls might blunt some of the worst economic components of the capital strike.



@propaganda
title: Launch a propaganda campaign blaming the guild-masters for the crisis.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: (radio >= 2 or commercialized_media >= 3) and resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if radio < 2 and commercialized_media < 3 : We have not built up our media enough. ?] [? if resources < 1: We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: commons_marcher += 7*(1-dissent); burgher_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); disfavored_marcher += 6*(1-dissent); pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We launch a counter-propaganda campaign to blame the economic crisis on the guild-masters, using all of our media channels to do so. Because of our existing media framework, this is moderately successful in directing popular criticisms towards the guild-masters and away from us.


@nothing
title: There is nothing we can do.

There is nothing we can do that is within constitutional and legal bounds.
